      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 43-year-old woman with no risk factors received mediastinal radiotherapy of 35 Grays at the age of 23 years for Hodgkin's disease, followed by cure of the neoplastic disease. Twenty years later, following a threatened infarction syndrome, coronary angiography revealed ostial stenosis of the left coronary trunk. The course was rapidly unfavourable immediately following the examination."},
